{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And Reuben went.</b> When he saw that his mother was distressed over having ceased bearing children." "<b>And he found mandrakes.</b> A species of fragrant herb that prepares the reproductive organs for conception, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated concerning the שׁוּם (Bava Kamma 82b) — and for this reason they would eat it on the eve of Sabbath. And likewise the mandrake species, or something superior to it, when combined also increase desire for conjugal union, as it says (Song of Songs 7:13–14): שָׁם אֶתֵּן אֶת דּוֹדַי לָךְ, הַדּוּדָאִים נָתְנוּ רֵיחַ. Through this Scripture informs us of Reuben's righteousness and wisdom, though he was then only four or five years old at most."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:28.445413424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}